      "writtenOn": "2022-08-25T15:04:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here you\u0027ve essentially written an RAII class and then wrapped it in another one. We only need one level of that.\n\nOne way to do it is with `SkAutoTCallVProc`, which is used elsewhere in this file. That was a Skia template before we moved to C++11 everywhere. You could also do something like:\n\n```\nstruct Deleter {\n    void operator()(WebPAnimEncoder* encoder) { WebPAnimEncoderDelete(encoder); }\n}\n\nstd::unique_ptr\u003cWebPAnimEncoder, Deleter\u003e encoderMgr;\n```\n\nI don\u0027t have a strong preference between the two. Using the struct allows saving a little bit of memory, though it\u0027s negligible in this case. (I don\u0027t know whether the Skia template also does that.)",
